{"name":"Golden Crest","hex":"#f6ca69","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"golden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of, or relating to, gold.","Having a color or other richness suggestive of gold."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["(Can we verify this sense?) brassy drummer, brassy chub, etc. (Kyphosus vaigiensis), a fish found in southeast Asia.","Ellipsis of golden retriever."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/golden"},{"term":"crest","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The summit of a hill or mountain ridge.","A tuft, or other natural ornament, growing on an animal's head, for example the comb of a cockerel, the swelling on the head of a snake, the lengthened feathers of the crown or nape of bird, etc."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Particularly with reference to waves, to reach a peak.","To reach the crest of (e.g. a hill or mountain)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crest"}],"entries":[{"title":"Golden Crest","blocks":[{"text":"The Golden Crest was a greyhound racing competition held annually at Poole Stadium."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golden_Crest"},{"title":"Hamilton Township, Mercer County, New Jersey","blocks":[{"text":"Hamilton Township is a township and the most populous municipality in Mercer County, in the U.S. state of New Jersey. It is the largest suburb of Trenton, the state's capital, which is located to the township's west. The township is situated within the New York metropolitan area as defined by the United States Census Bureau but directly borders the Philadelphia metropolitan area and is part of the Federal Communications Commission's Philadelphia Designated Market Area. As of the 2020 United States census, the township's population was 92,297, its highest decennial count ever and an increase of 3,833 (+4.3%) from the 2010 census count of 88,464, which in turn reflected an increase of 1,355 (+1.6%) from the 2000 census count of 87,109. The township was the state's ninth-largest municipality in 2010 and 2020, after having been ranked 10th in 2000."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Sayen_Park_%287058927789%29.jpg/330px-Sayen_Park_%287058927789%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hamilton_Township%2C_Mercer_County%2C_New_Jersey"},{"title":"Gold (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Gold, also called golden, is a color tone resembling the chemical element gold."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg/330px-GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/1988_Peasedown_Slippy_greyhound_racing.png/120px-1988_Peasedown_Slippy_greyhound_racing.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/57/1988_Peasedown_Slippy_greyhound_racing.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/1988_Peasedown_Slippy_greyhound_racing.png/120px-1988_Peasedown_Slippy_greyhound_racing.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A1988_Peasedown_Slippy_greyhound_racing.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/b/b3/Hamilton_Seal.png/120px-Hamilton_Seal.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b3/Hamilton_Seal.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/b/b3/Hamilton_Seal.png/120px-Hamilton_Seal.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_conten